487fca5cb04c45524aa3efde84fcd10ff0579e" commit="b9ac073c7966b107279fca2648cd5a8cf18156f4" commit_message="reef: enable tcpc-controlled drp toggle  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54668 BRANCH=none TEST=Verified SNK is detected in S0 (toggle on), S3 (toggle off), and S5 (force sink). SRC is detect in S0 only, stays detected when entered S3, but unplug/plug while in S3 will not re-detect until system back in S0. When go to S5, SRC will get disconnected until back in S0, and hotplug SRC in S5 will not get detected. Checked power role swap with another chromebook in the above scenario also.  Change-Id: I2a487fca5cb04c45524aa3efde84fcd10ff0579e Signed-off-by: Kevin K Wong &lt;kevin.k.wong@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/396918 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="396918" owner_email="kevin.k.wong@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/18/396918/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I9608615f3b7b91debb6157fc08d1fa2d2044d3ce" commit="d6b3e830a8893a5d652f3af0f3d9564b9acbbd67" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iommu/rockchip: Stop using pm_runtime_no_callbacks()  We found that when pm_runtime_no_callback() is called, it causes genpd callbacks to be bypassed as well. Moreover, some code, such as pm_runtime_force_suspend() or pm_runtime_force_resume(), does not even respect the power.no_callbacks flag and checks the callback pointers directly. Since our use case of pm_runtime_no_callback() did not even fully match the definition of this feature (our IOMMU does not have a parent device, in terms of kernel driver model, that would manage its power), let's just stop calling it and provide empty callbacks.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58891 TEST=Run few iterations of suspend_stress_test, check that enable count   of dclk_vop0 does not increase  Suggested-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Change-Id: I9608615f3b7b91debb6157fc08d1fa2d2044d3ce Signed-off-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/403691 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="403691" owner_email="tfiga@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/403691/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I82280023e09c164d7f861b4363bb68fab15ddb39" commit="016d91ca28695e1dd20b3f1ac2769a4589ab7ada" commit_message="Create an Android Telephony test suite  This will only be for the Verizon Nexus suite.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I82280023e09c164d7f861b4363bb68fab15ddb39 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405756 Commit-Ready: Kris Rambish &lt;krisr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kris Rambish &lt;krisr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kris Rambish &lt;krisr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="405756" owner_email="krisr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/56/405756/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I20ce4143903b41584f4f87853b4317f9818380ec" commit="36a95d8333d4c56de7f8dda8f7fb4ec8662e480e" commit_message="e2fsprogs, e2fsprogs-libs: upgraded packages to upstream  Upgraded sys-fs/e2fsprogs to version 1.43.3-r1 for all Upgraded sys-libs/e2fsprogs-libs to version 1.43.3 for all  https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/portage/+log/gentoo is three weeks old (chromium:660449), so this patch was generated by pointing the `cros_portage_upgrade` tool to a local copy of the gentoo github repo (git@github.com:gentoo/gentoo.git).  Command run: cros_portage_upgrade --upgrade --bo