ect="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/18/405818/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4fcfeec0fb13000637662028fd076a1539b8302d" commit="0d78c5f764f1cf800d2dece783f2cc26657eb87f" commit_message="vpd: Delimit RO and RW VPD in dump_vpd_log.  Add a delimiter between RO_VDP and RW_VPD output to allow for stronger consistency checks between VPD cache and actual VPD contents.  BUG=chromium:659029 TEST=manual  Change-Id: I4fcfeec0fb13000637662028fd076a1539b8302d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/403850 Commit-Ready: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="403850" owner_email="tnagel@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vpd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vpd" ref="refs/changes/50/403850/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5a9463bb0929104b83636250a8684c285502d0db" commit="c576045aa48364683f39aad7a06b961032e6a9b0" commit_message="moblab: Setup gsutil credentials for apache user.  RPC calls are executed by the apache user - to get RPC code to be able to access Google Cloud Storage they need the same credentials as the moblab user.  On startup link the moblab boto file to the apache user home directory.  Also create the .gsutil directory as the apache user can not create directories in /var/www  BUG=chromium:656131 TEST=build dev build and clean install on moblab, tested the user was setup correctly, works as expected in RPC calls, and that the code works on second boot up also after powerwash.  Change-Id: I5a9463bb0929104b83636250a8684c285502d0db Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405784 Commit-Ready: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="405784" owner_email="haddowk@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/84/405784/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Ie112104035b01166217a8c5b5586972b4d7ca6ec" commit="5f8d999bf88d63a6cdf5438f20872d1731391643" commit_message="rockchip/rk3399: Change PLL configuration to match Linux kernel  The Kevin project has been too smooth and boring for our tastes in the last last few weeks, so we've decided to stir the pot a little bit and reshuffle all our PLL settings at the last minute. The new settings match exactly what the Linux kernel expects on boot, so it doesn't need to reinitialize anything and risk a glitch.  Naturally, changing PLL rates will affect child clocks, so this patch changes vop_aclk (192MHz -&gt; 200MHz, 400MHz in the kernel), pmu_pclk (99MHz -&gt; 96.57MHz) and i2c0_src (198MHz -&gt; 338MHz, leading to an effective I2C0 change 399193Hz -&gt; 398584Hz).  BRANCH=gru BUG=chrome-os-partner:59139 TEST=Booted Kevin, sanity checking display and beep. Instrumented rockchip_rk3399_pll_set_params() in the kernel and confirmed that GPLL, PPLL and CPLL do not get reinitialized anymore (with additional kernel patch to ignore frac divider when it's not used). Also confirmed that /sys/kernel/debug/clk_summary now shows pclk_pmu_src 96571429 because the kernel doesn't even bother to reinitialize the divisor.  Change-Id: Ie112104035b01166217a8c5b5586972b4d7ca6ec Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405785 Commit-Ready: Xing Zheng &lt;zhengxing@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Xing Zheng &lt;zhengxing@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Xing Zheng &lt;zhengxing@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="405785" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/85/405785/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8953.0.0-rc10"/></manifest>